  # Why: Just-inside boundary — the smallest meaningful runbook has exactly one step
  @task:TASK-RSP-003
  @boundary
  Scenario: A runbook with a single step is created and loaded
    Given a runbook for a target with exactly one step
    When I create the runbook and load it back
    Then the loaded runbook should contain exactly that one step
    And the resume pointer should point at the only step

  # Why: Just-outside boundary — a runbook with no steps has nothing to execute
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] A runbook must contain at least one step; creating one with an empty step list is refused.
  @task:TASK-RSP-003
  @boundary @negative
