  @task:TASK-RSP-005
  @edge-case
  Scenario Outline: Adversarial identifiers and target round-trip verbatim through the runbook store
    Given a runbook whose identifier is "<identifier>" and whose target is "<target>" with a step whose step type is "<step_type>"
    When the runbook is persisted to the runbook store
    And the runbook is loaded back from the runbook store
    Then the loaded runbook reports its identifier as exactly "<identifier>"
    And the loaded runbook reports its target as exactly "<target>"
    And the loaded step reports its step type as exactly "<step_type>"

    Examples:
      | identifier          | target         | step_type             |
      | ../../etc/passwd    | ../../../root  | run; DROP TABLE steps |
